IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`
IMPORT `fhog-terms`
IMPORT `taa-procedure`
IMPORT `sda-home`
IMPORT `sda-vehicles`
IMPORT `fhog-grant`

-- Stamp Duties Act 1923 (SA), with the First Home and Housing Construction Grants Act 2000, its Regulations 2015, the
-- Stamp Duties Regulations 2013 and the Taxation Administration Act 1996 -- the buyer's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the buyer of a home or a car in South Australia -- including the first home buyer applying for the s 71DD relief
-- and the first home owner grant. "What duty do I pay on my home? Does a new home or land cost me nothing? What must I do
-- to keep that relief, and what if I don't? Is the grant payable, how much, by when do I apply, when must I repay it?
-- What duty is on registering my car?" Every question is phrased as that person would ask it, on facts that person could
-- state. The rules are in sda-home.l4, fhog-grant.l4, fhog-terms.l4, sda-vehicles.l4 and taa-procedure.l4; this module
-- builds their records from plain answers and restates no rule.
--
-- GENERATED by scratchpad au-sa-1/gen_seat.py so that each question carries the same seat-worded inputs.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken through
-- the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0). NOT the official texts; as at 2025-02-13 (the two Acts), 2022-09-29 and
-- 2021-03-11 (the Regulations) and 2019-10-03 (Taxation Administration Act); they may be out of date. BASELINE. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Stamp Duties Act 1923 and First Home and Housing Construction Grants Act 2000 (SA) -- the buyer's questions`

§§ `Building the core's records from plain answers`

-- What is bought (s 71DD(1), (13)): a new home in the FHOG Act's sense (s 3), being a home (s 4), or vacant land. The
-- s 4 opinion of the Commissioner ("a suitable building for use as a place of residence") is taken as given: the
-- answer holds if the Commissioner is of that opinion.

GIVEN `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you are buying includes a building fixed to the land that may lawfully be used as a place of residence (a home); answer no for vacant land
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has previously been occupied or sold as a place of residence (answer no for a brand-new home)
      `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home was substantially renovated and its sale to you is a taxable supply of new residential premises under the GST Act s 40-75(1)(b)
      `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home, as renovated, has been occupied or sold as a place of residence before your purchase
      `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying vacant land on which a home is to be built
GIVETH A `What is bought`
`what I am buying, from my answers` `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation` `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built` MEANS
    IF `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built`
    THEN `vacant land on which a home is to be built`
    ELSE IF     `the building is a home (s 4)` `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in` `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in` TRUE
            AND `the home is a new home (s 3)` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation`
         THEN `a new home`
         ELSE `something else`

GIVEN `the date of the contract`                                                  IS A DATE @desc The day you entered into the contract to buy, as a date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `the market value when the contract was made`                               IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of the home and its land (or of the vacant land) on the day the contract was made, in Australian dollars (usually the price)
      `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you are buying includes a building fixed to the land that may lawfully be used as a place of residence (a home); answer no for vacant land
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has previously been occupied or sold as a place of residence (answer no for a brand-new home)
      `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home was substantially renovated and its sale to you is a taxable supply of new residential premises under the GST Act s 40-75(1)(b)
      `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home, as renovated, has been occupied or sold as a place of residence before your purchase
      `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying vacant land on which a home is to be built
      `every buyer is 18 or older`                                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-buyer is at least 18 (or the Commissioner has determined under s 71DD(6) that the relief applies anyway)
      `at least one buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or at least one co-buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident (holds a permanent visa, or is a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa) when you apply
      `a buyer or partner has had this relief before`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-buyer or a spouse or domestic partner of any of you has been a party to an earlier purchase that got this relief (a spouse you are separated from, with no intention of resuming, does not count)
      `a buyer or partner has owned residential property before`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-buyer or a spouse or domestic partner of any of you held a relevant interest (usually ownership) in residential property in South Australia or another State or Territory before the contract
      `one of us lived in that property for 6 months in a row`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether whoever owned that earlier property lived in it as a place of residence for at least 6 months in a row (it matters only for a contract made before the relevant day)
      `the relevant day`                                                          IS A DATE @desc The day the Statutes Amendment (Budget Measures) Act 2025 was assented to (the deposited legislative history records 13 February 2025), as a date (ISO 8601)
      `every buyer is an individual`                                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-buyer is an individual (a natural person), not a company or a trust
      `every owner after the transfer is applying`                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether everyone who will own the home or land after the transfer is joining in the application for the relief
      `the contract replaces an earlier one for the same property`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied your contract replaces an earlier contract for the same home or land made before 15 June 2023 (for a contract made before 6 June 2024) or before 6 June 2024 (for a later contract)
GIVETH A `New home purchase`
`my purchase, from my answers` `the date of the contract` `the market value when the contract was made` `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation` `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built` `every buyer is 18 or older` `at least one buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `a buyer or partner has had this relief before` `a buyer or partner has owned residential property before` `one of us lived in that property for 6 months in a row` `the relevant day` `every buyer is an individual` `every owner after the transfer is applying` `the contract replaces an earlier one for the same property` MEANS
    `New home purchase` WITH
        `what is bought`                                                                                                    IS `what I am buying, from my answers` `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation` `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built`
        `the date the contract was entered into`                                                                            IS `the date of the contract`
        `the market value when the contract was entered into`                                                               IS `the market value when the contract was made`
        `every purchaser is at least 18, or the Commissioner so determines under s 71DD(6)`                                 IS `every buyer is 18 or older`
        `at least one purchaser is an Australian citizen or permanent resident when applying`                               IS `at least one buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`
        `a purchaser or spouse was a party to an earlier conveyance relieved under s 71DD(2)`                               IS `a buyer or partner has had this relief before`
        `a purchaser or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property in SA or another State before the contract` IS `a buyer or partner has owned residential property before`
        `a purchaser or spouse occupied that property as a residence for 6 continuous months`                               IS `one of us lived in that property for 6 months in a row`
        `the relevant day`                                                                                                  IS `the relevant day`
        `every applicant is a natural person`                                                                               IS `every buyer is an individual`
        `every owner after the transfer joins in the application`                                                           IS `every owner after the transfer is applying`
        `the Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces an earlier contract for the same home or land`                 IS `the contract replaces an earlier one for the same property`

GIVEN `the price`                                         IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying for the property, in Australian dollars (0 if it is a gift)
      `the market value of the property`                  IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of the property on the day of the transfer, free of any mortgage or other encumbrance, in Australian dollars (if you do not know it, give the price)
      `I am buying it`                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying the property (a sale), rather than receiving it as a gift
      `the Commissioner will take the price as the value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner of State Taxation will take the price as the value (s 60A(2)): usually yes for an ordinary sale at market price; not where it appears the price may be less than the market value
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of my property, from my answers` `the price` `the market value of the property` `I am buying it` `the Commissioner will take the price as the value` MEANS
    `the value of the property conveyed (s 60A)` `the market value of the property` `the price` `I am buying it` `the Commissioner will take the price as the value`

-- The grant's kind of transaction: a purchase; an owner builder; otherwise a comprehensive home building contract.

GIVEN `I am buying the home under a contract of sale`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying the home (with its land) under a contract of sale; answer no if you are having it built or building it yourself
      `I am building the home myself as an owner builder`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are building the home (or having it built) on your land without a comprehensive home building contract (an owner builder)
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has previously been occupied or sold as a place of residence (answer no for a brand-new home)
      `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home was substantially renovated and its sale to you is a taxable supply of new residential premises under the GST Act s 40-75(1)(b)
      `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home, as renovated, has been occupied or sold as a place of residence before your purchase
      `the commencement date`                                                     IS A DATE @desc The day the contract was made, or for an owner builder the day laying the foundations began (ISO 8601)
      `the transaction is complete`                                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transaction is complete: for a purchase, you are entitled to possession and the steps to register your title have been taken; for a building, it is ready to live in
      `the date of completion`                                                    IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction was (or will be) completed (ISO 8601)
      `the consideration`                                                         IS A NUMBER @desc The price of the home (for a purchase), the total price of the building work (for a building contract), or your actual costs excluding your own labour (for an owner builder), in Australian dollars
      `the Commissioner thinks the price may be below market value`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a purchase: whether the Commissioner considers the price may be less than the market value
      `the market value as the Commissioner determines it`                        IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of the home and land as the Commissioner determines it (used for a building contract, an owner builder, or a purchase the Commissioner thinks is under-priced), in Australian dollars; otherwise the price
      `the Commissioner thinks it is a scheme to get around the rules`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is of the opinion the transaction forms part of a scheme to circumvent the grant's limits or requirements
      `every applicant is an individual`                                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-applicant is an individual (a natural person)
      `every applicant is 18 or older`                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-applicant is at least 18 (or the Commissioner has exempted you)
      `at least one applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or at least one co-applicant is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident
      `an applicant or partner has had a grant before`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-applicant or a spouse or domestic partner of any of you was a party to an earlier first home owner grant application, in any State, on which a grant was paid (a separated spouse does not count)
      `that grant was repaid for not living in the home, with any penalty paid`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that earlier grant was paid back because the residence requirement or a condition was not met, and any s 39(3) penalty was paid
      `an applicant or partner could have had a grant on an earlier purchase`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-applicant or a partner could have successfully applied for a first home owner grant on an earlier transaction (or could have, had you then been a citizen or permanent resident)
      `an applicant or partner owned residential property before 1 July 2000`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-applicant or a partner held a relevant interest (usually ownership) in residential property in Australia before 1 July 2000
      `an applicant or partner has owned residential property`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-applicant or a partner held a relevant interest (usually ownership) in residential property in Australia before the commencement date
      `whoever owned it lived in it for 6 months in a row`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether whoever owned that property lived in it as a place of residence for at least 6 months in a row (it matters only before the relevant day)
      `the relevant day for the grant`                                            IS A DATE @desc The day section 4 of the Statutes Amendment (Budget Measures) Act 2025 came into operation (the deposited legislative history records 13 February 2025), as a date (ISO 8601)
      `every owner is applying`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether everyone who is, or on completion will be, an owner of the home is an applicant
      `the date I apply`                                                          IS A DATE @desc The day you apply (or applied) for the grant (ISO 8601)
      `the Commissioner allows my application outside the period`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has allowed your application before or after the application period
GIVETH A `Grant application`
`my grant application, from my answers` `I am buying the home under a contract of sale` `I am building the home myself as an owner builder` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation` `the commencement date` `the transaction is complete` `the date of completion` `the consideration` `the Commissioner thinks the price may be below market value` `the market value as the Commissioner determines it` `the Commissioner thinks it is a scheme to get around the rules` `every applicant is an individual` `every applicant is 18 or older` `at least one applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `an applicant or partner has had a grant before` `that grant was repaid for not living in the home, with any penalty paid` `an applicant or partner could have had a grant on an earlier purchase` `an applicant or partner owned residential property before 1 July 2000` `an applicant or partner has owned residential property` `whoever owned it lived in it for 6 months in a row` `the relevant day for the grant` `every owner is applying` `the date I apply` `the Commissioner allows my application outside the period` MEANS
    `Grant application` WITH
        `the kind of transaction`                                                                              IS `the kind of my transaction`
        `the home is a new home`                                                                               IS `the home is a new home (s 3)` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation`
        `the commencement date`                                                                                IS `the commencement date`
        `the transaction has been completed`                                                                   IS `the transaction is complete`
        `the date of completion`                                                                               IS `the date of completion`
        `the consideration`                                                                                    IS `the consideration`
        `the Commissioner considers the consideration may be less than the market value`                       IS `the Commissioner thinks the price may be below market value`
        `the market value as determined by the Commissioner`                                                   IS `the market value as the Commissioner determines it`
        `the Commissioner is of the opinion it is a scheme to circumvent the Act`                              IS `the Commissioner thinks it is a scheme to get around the rules`
        `every applicant is a natural person`                                                                  IS `every applicant is an individual`
        `every applicant is at least 18, or exempted by the Commissioner`                                      IS `every applicant is 18 or older`
        `at least one applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`                                IS `at least one applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`
        `an applicant or spouse was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid`               IS `an applicant or partner has had a grant before`
        `that grant was repaid for a residence or condition failure, with any s 39(3) penalty paid`            IS `that grant was repaid for not living in the home, with any penalty paid`
        `an applicant or spouse could have successfully applied for a grant on an earlier transaction`         IS `an applicant or partner could have had a grant on an earlier purchase`
        `an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000`           IS `an applicant or partner owned residential property before 1 July 2000`
        `an applicant or spouse held a relevant interest in residential property before the commencement date` IS `an applicant or partner has owned residential property`
        `an applicant or spouse occupied that property as a residence for 6 continuous months`                 IS `whoever owned it lived in it for 6 months in a row`
        `the relevant day`                                                                                     IS `the relevant day for the grant`
        `every interested person is an applicant`                                                              IS `every owner is applying`
        `the date of the application`                                                                          IS `the date I apply`
        `the Commissioner allows the application outside the application period`                               IS `the Commissioner allows my application outside the period`
    WHERE
        `the kind of my transaction` MEANS
            IF `I am buying the home under a contract of sale`
            THEN `a contract for the purchase of a home in the State`
            ELSE IF `I am building the home myself as an owner builder`
                 THEN `the building of a home in the State by an owner builder`
                 ELSE `a comprehensive home building contract for a home in the State`

GIVEN `it is a trailer that is not a heavy vehicle`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a trailer that is not a heavy vehicle
      `ad valorem duty already paid on buying it`              IS A NUMBER @desc Ad valorem stamp duty already paid or payable on another document by which the vehicle was transferred to you, in Australian dollars; otherwise 0
      `I am entitled to the s 38 reduced registration fee`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled under section 38 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 to register the vehicle at a reduced fee
      `I already have this exemption on another vehicle I own` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you already enjoy the s 38 duty exemption on another vehicle you currently own
      `I own the vehicle`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the owner of the vehicle
      `I hold a South Australian concession card`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a State concession card issued by the department responsible for the Family and Community Services Act 1972 (the class prescribed by Stamp Duties Regulations 2013 reg 14)
      `I hold a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a pensioner entitlement card issued under a Commonwealth law (for example a Pensioner Concession Card)
      `my card gives me reduced public transport fares`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that card entitles you to travel on public transport in South Australia at reduced fares
GIVETH A `Vehicle exemption facts`
`my vehicle exemption facts, from my answers` `it is a trailer that is not a heavy vehicle` `ad valorem duty already paid on buying it` `I am entitled to the s 38 reduced registration fee` `I already have this exemption on another vehicle I own` `I own the vehicle` `I hold a South Australian concession card` `I hold a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card` `my card gives me reduced public transport fares` MEANS
    `Vehicle exemption facts` WITH
        `it is a trailer that is not a heavy vehicle`                                       IS `it is a trailer that is not a heavy vehicle`
        `ad valorem duty paid or payable on another instrument transferring the vehicle`    IS `ad valorem duty already paid on buying it`
        `the applicant is entitled under MVA s 38 to a reduced registration fee`            IS `I am entitled to the s 38 reduced registration fee`
        `the applicant enjoys exemption 11 or policy exemption 6 for another vehicle owned` IS `I already have this exemption on another vehicle I own`
        `the applicant owns the vehicle`                                                    IS `I own the vehicle`
        `the applicant holds a State concession card of the prescribed class`               IS `I hold a South Australian concession card`
        `the applicant holds a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card`                     IS `I hold a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card`
        `the card entitles the applicant to reduced public transport fares in the State`    IS `my card gives me reduced public transport fares`

GIVEN `I am registering the vehicle`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying to register (or renew the registration of) the vehicle; answer no if you are applying to transfer its registration into your name
      `it is a new vehicle with a list price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle has never been registered anywhere and has a manufacturer's or distributor's list price in South Australia
      `I bought it second-hand`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are transferring the registration of a previously registered vehicle that you bought
GIVETH A `Kind of vehicle application`
`the kind of my vehicle application, from my answers` `I am registering the vehicle` `it is a new vehicle with a list price` `I bought it second-hand` MEANS
    IF `I am registering the vehicle` AND `it is a new vehicle with a list price`
    THEN `registering a new motor vehicle that has a list price`
    ELSE IF (NOT `I am registering the vehicle`) AND `I bought it second-hand`
         THEN `transferring the registration of a second-hand motor vehicle on its sale`
         ELSE `any other application`

GIVEN `the registration period, in months`         IS A NUMBER @desc The period of registration you are applying for, in months, counting part of a month as a month (12 for a year)
      `the registration period is 31 days or less` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the period of registration is 31 days or less
GIVETH A `Period of registration`
`my registration period, from my answers` `the registration period, in months` `the registration period is 31 days or less` MEANS
    IF `the registration period is 31 days or less`
    THEN `not more than 31 days`
    ELSE IF `the registration period, in months` EQUALS 12
         THEN `12 months`
         ELSE IF `the registration period, in months` GREATER THAN 12
              THEN `more than 12 months`
              ELSE `more than 31 days but less than 12 months` `the registration period, in months`

GIVEN `I told the Commissioner in writing before any audit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you disclosed the failure in writing to the Commissioner before you were notified of a tax audit
      `I told the Commissioner in writing during an audit`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you disclosed the failure in writing while subject to a tax audit
      `I obstructed an audit`                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or someone for you obstructed a tax audit (refused to comply with a requirement, hindered an officer or destroyed records)
GIVETH A `Taxpayer conduct`
`my conduct, from my answers` `I told the Commissioner in writing before any audit` `I told the Commissioner in writing during an audit` `I obstructed an audit` MEANS
    IF `I told the Commissioner in writing before any audit`
    THEN `a sufficient disclosure while not subject to a tax audit`
    ELSE IF `I told the Commissioner in writing during an audit`
         THEN `a sufficient disclosure while subject to a tax audit`
         ELSE IF `I obstructed an audit`
              THEN `obstructive conduct while subject to a tax audit`
              ELSE `no disclosure and no obstruction`

§§ `Buying a home -- the duty`

@export What stamp duty (conveyance duty on the Schedule 2 general scale) is charged on the home or land I am buying in South Australia, before any relief?
GIVEN `the price`                                         IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying for the property, in Australian dollars (0 if it is a gift)
      `the market value of the property`                  IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of the property on the day of the transfer, free of any mortgage or other encumbrance, in Australian dollars (if you do not know it, give the price)
      `I am buying it`                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying the property (a sale), rather than receiving it as a gift
      `the Commissioner will take the price as the value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner of State Taxation will take the price as the value (s 60A(2)): usually yes for an ordinary sale at market price; not where it appears the price may be less than the market value
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What duty is charged on my home before any relief` IS
    `the conveyance duty on the general scale` (`the value of my property, from my answers` `the price` `the market value of the property` `I am buying it` `the Commissioner will take the price as the value`)

-- Situation: buying out, or transferring to, a spouse or domestic partner. Ask first "Is the transfer between you and
-- your partner or former partner?"
@export Is the transfer of our home between me and my spouse or domestic partner (current, or former after a breakdown) exempt from stamp duty (s 71CB)?
GIVEN `it is or was our principal place of residence`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home is your and your partner's principal place of residence (or, if you have separated, was your last one)
      `one or both of us owns or owned it`                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one or both of you is (or, for former partners, was) an owner of the home
      `it is part of industrial or commercial premises`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home forms part of industrial or commercial premises
      `the only effect is to transfer the home between us`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the sole effect of the transfer is to transfer an interest in the home between you and your spouse or domestic partner (current or former)
      `we are spouses or domestic partners`                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are legally married to, or the domestic partner of, the other party now
      `we were spouses or domestic partners and have separated`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were married to, or the domestic partner of, the other party and the relationship has ended
      `the Commissioner accepts it is because the relationship broke down` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For former partners: whether the Commissioner is satisfied the transfer was made as a result of the irretrievable breakdown of the marriage or relationship
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the transfer of our home between us exempt` IS
    `the transfer of the home is exempt (s 71CB(2)(a)(i))` `the only effect is to transfer the home between us` (`the premises are a shared residence (s 71CB(1))` `it is or was our principal place of residence` `one or both of us owns or owned it` `it is part of industrial or commercial premises`) `relationship` `the Commissioner accepts it is because the relationship broke down`
    WHERE
        `relationship` MEANS
            IF `we are spouses or domestic partners`
            THEN `spouses or domestic partners`
            ELSE IF `we were spouses or domestic partners and have separated`
                 THEN `former spouses or former domestic partners`
                 ELSE `neither`

@export By what date must the stamp duty be paid and the transfer stamped (s 20(1))?
GIVEN `the date the transfer was signed`       IS A DATE @desc The day the transfer or contract was signed (executed), as a date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `it was signed in South Australia`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transfer or contract was signed in South Australia
      `the date it arrived in South Australia` IS A DATE @desc If it was signed outside South Australia, the day it was received in South Australia (ISO 8601); otherwise any date
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the duty be paid and the transfer stamped` IS
    `the last day to pay the duty and stamp the instrument (s 20(1))` `the date the transfer was signed` `where`
    WHERE
        `where` MEANS
            IF `it was signed in South Australia`
            THEN `in South Australia`
            ELSE `outside South Australia` `the date it arrived in South Australia`

@export What is the most I can be fined, in dollars, if the transfer I signed is not stamped in time (s 20(4)-(6))?
GIVEN `it was produced for stamping in time`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transfer was produced to the Commissioner for stamping within the period (usually two months after signing)
      `it was duly stamped another authorised way in time`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transfer was duly stamped in time in another way the Stamp Duties Act authorises (for example through electronic conveyancing with a stamp duty certificate)
      `I handed it to the other party expecting them to have it stamped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you delivered the transfer to another party to it, or their agent (for example the other side's conveyancer), reasonably expecting them to have it stamped
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for not stamping in time` IS
    `the most the person who executed it can be fined (s 20(4)-(6))` `it was produced for stamping in time` `it was duly stamped another authorised way in time` `I handed it to the other party expecting them to have it stamped`

§§ `Buying a new home or land to build on -- the relief (s 71DD)`

-- Situation: buying a new home, or vacant land to build a home on, under a contract made on or after 15 June 2023.

@export Do I qualify for the stamp duty relief on a new home or vacant land to build on (Stamp Duties Act s 71DD)?
GIVEN `the date of the contract`                                                  IS A DATE @desc The day you entered into the contract to buy, as a date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `the market value when the contract was made`                               IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of the home and its land (or of the vacant land) on the day the contract was made, in Australian dollars (usually the price)
      `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you are buying includes a building fixed to the land that may lawfully be used as a place of residence (a home); answer no for vacant land
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has previously been occupied or sold as a place of residence (answer no for a brand-new home)
      `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home was substantially renovated and its sale to you is a taxable supply of new residential premises under the GST Act s 40-75(1)(b)
      `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home, as renovated, has been occupied or sold as a place of residence before your purchase
      `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying vacant land on which a home is to be built
      `every buyer is 18 or older`                                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-buyer is at least 18 (or the Commissioner has determined under s 71DD(6) that the relief applies anyway)
      `at least one buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or at least one co-buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident (holds a permanent visa, or is a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa) when you apply
      `a buyer or partner has had this relief before`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-buyer or a spouse or domestic partner of any of you has been a party to an earlier purchase that got this relief (a spouse you are separated from, with no intention of resuming, does not count)
      `a buyer or partner has owned residential property before`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-buyer or a spouse or domestic partner of any of you held a relevant interest (usually ownership) in residential property in South Australia or another State or Territory before the contract
      `one of us lived in that property for 6 months in a row`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether whoever owned that earlier property lived in it as a place of residence for at least 6 months in a row (it matters only for a contract made before the relevant day)
      `the relevant day`                                                          IS A DATE @desc The day the Statutes Amendment (Budget Measures) Act 2025 was assented to (the deposited legislative history records 13 February 2025), as a date (ISO 8601)
      `every buyer is an individual`                                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-buyer is an individual (a natural person), not a company or a trust
      `every owner after the transfer is applying`                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether everyone who will own the home or land after the transfer is joining in the application for the relief
      `the contract replaces an earlier one for the same property`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied your contract replaces an earlier contract for the same home or land made before 15 June 2023 (for a contract made before 6 June 2024) or before 6 June 2024 (for a later contract)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I qualify for the relief on a new home or land` IS
    `s 71DD applies to the conveyance (s 71DD(1), (8), (9))` (`my purchase, from my answers` `the date of the contract` `the market value when the contract was made` `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation` `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built` `every buyer is 18 or older` `at least one buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `a buyer or partner has had this relief before` `a buyer or partner has owned residential property before` `one of us lived in that property for 6 months in a row` `the relevant day` `every buyer is an individual` `every owner after the transfer is applying` `the contract replaces an earlier one for the same property`)

@export How much stamp duty do I pay on my home or land after any s 71DD relief (nil for a qualifying contract from 6 June 2024)?
GIVEN `the price`                                                                 IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying for the property, in Australian dollars (0 if it is a gift)
      `the market value of the property`                                          IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of the property on the day of the transfer, free of any mortgage or other encumbrance, in Australian dollars (if you do not know it, give the price)
      `I am buying it`                                                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying the property (a sale), rather than receiving it as a gift
      `the Commissioner will take the price as the value`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner of State Taxation will take the price as the value (s 60A(2)): usually yes for an ordinary sale at market price; not where it appears the price may be less than the market value
      `the date of the contract`                                                  IS A DATE @desc The day you entered into the contract to buy, as a date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `the market value when the contract was made`                               IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of the home and its land (or of the vacant land) on the day the contract was made, in Australian dollars (usually the price)
      `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you are buying includes a building fixed to the land that may lawfully be used as a place of residence (a home); answer no for vacant land
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has previously been occupied or sold as a place of residence (answer no for a brand-new home)
      `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home was substantially renovated and its sale to you is a taxable supply of new residential premises under the GST Act s 40-75(1)(b)
      `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home, as renovated, has been occupied or sold as a place of residence before your purchase
      `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying vacant land on which a home is to be built
      `every buyer is 18 or older`                                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-buyer is at least 18 (or the Commissioner has determined under s 71DD(6) that the relief applies anyway)
      `at least one buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or at least one co-buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident (holds a permanent visa, or is a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa) when you apply
      `a buyer or partner has had this relief before`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-buyer or a spouse or domestic partner of any of you has been a party to an earlier purchase that got this relief (a spouse you are separated from, with no intention of resuming, does not count)
      `a buyer or partner has owned residential property before`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-buyer or a spouse or domestic partner of any of you held a relevant interest (usually ownership) in residential property in South Australia or another State or Territory before the contract
      `one of us lived in that property for 6 months in a row`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether whoever owned that earlier property lived in it as a place of residence for at least 6 months in a row (it matters only for a contract made before the relevant day)
      `the relevant day`                                                          IS A DATE @desc The day the Statutes Amendment (Budget Measures) Act 2025 was assented to (the deposited legislative history records 13 February 2025), as a date (ISO 8601)
      `every buyer is an individual`                                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-buyer is an individual (a natural person), not a company or a trust
      `every owner after the transfer is applying`                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether everyone who will own the home or land after the transfer is joining in the application for the relief
      `the contract replaces an earlier one for the same property`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied your contract replaces an earlier contract for the same home or land made before 15 June 2023 (for a contract made before 6 June 2024) or before 6 June 2024 (for a later contract)
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `How much duty do I pay after the relief` IS
    `the conveyance duty after the s 71DD relief` (`my purchase, from my answers` `the date of the contract` `the market value when the contract was made` `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation` `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built` `every buyer is 18 or older` `at least one buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `a buyer or partner has had this relief before` `a buyer or partner has owned residential property before` `one of us lived in that property for 6 months in a row` `the relevant day` `every buyer is an individual` `every owner after the transfer is applying` `the contract replaces an earlier one for the same property`) (`the conveyance duty on the general scale` (`the value of my property, from my answers` `the price` `the market value of the property` `I am buying it` `the Commissioner will take the price as the value`))

-- Situation: a buyer who is not an Australian citizen, permanent visa holder or New Zealand citizen with a special
-- category visa. The surcharge is assessed with the transfer (s 72(4)); the date of the contract stands for the date of
-- the instrument.
@export How much foreign ownership surcharge (7%, s 72) must I pay on the home or land, after any s 71DD relief?
GIVEN `the date of the contract`                                                  IS A DATE @desc The day you entered into the contract to buy, as a date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `I am an Australian citizen`                                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen
      `I hold a permanent visa`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a permanent visa under the Migration Act 1958
      `I am a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa
      `the Commissioner treats the land as residential land`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has determined (with the Valuer-General's information) that the land is residential land: used mainly for residential purposes, with residential improvements, or vacant land zoned residential
      `the value of my interest`                                                  IS A NUMBER @desc The value of the interest you acquire in the land, in Australian dollars (for a half share of a $600 000 home, $300 000)
      `the market value when the contract was made`                               IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of the home and its land (or of the vacant land) on the day the contract was made, in Australian dollars (usually the price)
      `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you are buying includes a building fixed to the land that may lawfully be used as a place of residence (a home); answer no for vacant land
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has previously been occupied or sold as a place of residence (answer no for a brand-new home)
      `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home was substantially renovated and its sale to you is a taxable supply of new residential premises under the GST Act s 40-75(1)(b)
      `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home, as renovated, has been occupied or sold as a place of residence before your purchase
      `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying vacant land on which a home is to be built
      `every buyer is 18 or older`                                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-buyer is at least 18 (or the Commissioner has determined under s 71DD(6) that the relief applies anyway)
      `at least one buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or at least one co-buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident (holds a permanent visa, or is a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa) when you apply
      `a buyer or partner has had this relief before`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-buyer or a spouse or domestic partner of any of you has been a party to an earlier purchase that got this relief (a spouse you are separated from, with no intention of resuming, does not count)
      `a buyer or partner has owned residential property before`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-buyer or a spouse or domestic partner of any of you held a relevant interest (usually ownership) in residential property in South Australia or another State or Territory before the contract
      `one of us lived in that property for 6 months in a row`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether whoever owned that earlier property lived in it as a place of residence for at least 6 months in a row (it matters only for a contract made before the relevant day)
      `the relevant day`                                                          IS A DATE @desc The day the Statutes Amendment (Budget Measures) Act 2025 was assented to (the deposited legislative history records 13 February 2025), as a date (ISO 8601)
      `every buyer is an individual`                                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-buyer is an individual (a natural person), not a company or a trust
      `every owner after the transfer is applying`                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether everyone who will own the home or land after the transfer is joining in the application for the relief
      `the contract replaces an earlier one for the same property`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied your contract replaces an earlier contract for the same home or land made before 15 June 2023 (for a contract made before 6 June 2024) or before 6 June 2024 (for a later contract)
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `How much foreign ownership surcharge must I pay` IS
    IF `the s 71DD relief extends to the foreign ownership surcharge` (`my purchase, from my answers` `the date of the contract` `the market value when the contract was made` `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation` `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built` `every buyer is 18 or older` `at least one buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `a buyer or partner has had this relief before` `a buyer or partner has owned residential property before` `one of us lived in that property for 6 months in a row` `the relevant day` `every buyer is an individual` `every owner after the transfer is applying` `the contract replaces an earlier one for the same property`)
    THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
    ELSE `the amount, in dollars, is` (`the foreign ownership surcharge (s 72)` `the date of the contract` `the Commissioner treats the land as residential land` (`the natural person is a foreign person (s 2(14)(a)(i))` `I am an Australian citizen` `I hold a permanent visa` `I am a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa`) `the value of my interest`)

§§ `Keeping the relief -- living in the home (s 71DD(4), s 71DE)`

-- Situation: you have had the s 71DD relief. Ask first "Did you get the relief on a new home or land?"

@export By what date must we begin living in the home as our principal place of residence to keep the s 71DD relief?
GIVEN `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you are buying includes a building fixed to the land that may lawfully be used as a place of residence (a home); answer no for vacant land
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has previously been occupied or sold as a place of residence (answer no for a brand-new home)
      `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home was substantially renovated and its sale to you is a taxable supply of new residential premises under the GST Act s 40-75(1)(b)
      `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home, as renovated, has been occupied or sold as a place of residence before your purchase
      `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying vacant land on which a home is to be built
      `the date of the transfer`                                                  IS A DATE @desc The day the transfer occurred (settlement), as a date (ISO 8601)
      `a home on the land can now lawfully be lived in`                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc For vacant land: whether a home built on it can now lawfully be used as a place of residence
      `the date a home on the land could first lawfully be lived in`              IS A DATE @desc For vacant land: the day you were first lawfully able to use the home built on it as a place of residence (ISO 8601); otherwise any date
      `a longer completion period approved by the Commissioner, in months`        IS A NUMBER @desc If the Commissioner has approved a longer time to move in, its length in months from the transfer; otherwise 0
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must we start living in the home to keep the relief` IS
    `the last day to begin the residence period (s 71DD(4), (5))` (`what I am buying, from my answers` `it is a dwelling fixed to the land that may lawfully be lived in` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation` `it is vacant land on which a home is to be built`) `the date of the transfer` `a home on the land can now lawfully be lived in` `the date a home on the land could first lawfully be lived in` `a longer completion period approved by the Commissioner, in months`

@export Until what date must we keep living in the home, without a break, to keep the s 71DD relief?
GIVEN `the date we moved in`                                               IS A DATE @desc The day you began to live in the home as your principal place of residence, as a date (ISO 8601)
      `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If the Commissioner has approved a residence period shorter than 6 months, its length in months; otherwise 0
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until when must we keep living in the home` IS
    `the day the residence period ends (s 71DD(4), (5))` `the date we moved in` `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner, in months`

@export If we lose the s 71DD relief, how much stamp duty becomes payable (at the rates in force at the transfer, s 71DE)?
GIVEN `the value of the property at the date of the transfer` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of the home or land for duty at the date of the transfer, in Australian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What duty becomes payable if we lose the relief` IS
    `the duty payable when the relief ceases (s 71DE(1), (2)(c), (d))` `the value of the property at the date of the transfer`

@export If we lose the s 71DD relief, by what date must the duty be paid and the transfer stamped (s 71DE(2)(e), s 20(2))?
GIVEN `the date the relief ended` IS A DATE @desc The day the relief ended: the day you failed the residence requirement (for example moved out early), or the day the Commissioner ceased to be satisfied you qualify (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the duty be paid once the relief is lost` IS
    `the last day to pay duty that becomes chargeable after execution (s 20(2))` `the date the relief ended`

@export What is the most interest and penalty tax I can be charged, in dollars, on the duty when the s 71DD relief is lost (s 71DE(2)(f), Taxation Administration Act Part 5)?
GIVEN `the duty that became payable`                                              IS A NUMBER @desc The duty payable once the relief is lost, in Australian dollars
      `the Commissioner charges interest and penalty tax`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner, in the Commissioner's discretion, makes you liable for interest and penalty tax on that duty (s 71DE(2)(f))
      `the days from the transfer until I pay`                                    IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from the date of the transfer to the day you pay the duty
      `the market rate`                                                           IS A NUMBER @desc The market rate for the financial year, per cent a year (the May average of the 90-day Bank Accepted Bill Rate, or a rate the Minister gazettes), e.g. 4.35
      `the failure was deliberate`                                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the failure to pay was deliberate (a deliberate act or omission by you or someone acting for you)
      `the Commissioner accepts it was not deliberate and I took reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied the failure was not deliberate and did not result from any failure to take reasonable care
      `I told the Commissioner in writing before any audit`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you disclosed the failure in writing to the Commissioner before you were notified of a tax audit
      `I told the Commissioner in writing during an audit`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you disclosed the failure in writing while subject to a tax audit
      `I obstructed an audit`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or someone for you obstructed a tax audit (refused to comply with a requirement, hindered an officer or destroyed records)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most interest and penalty tax when the relief is lost` IS
    `the most interest and penalty tax when the relief ceases (s 71DE(2)(f))` `the duty that became payable` `the Commissioner charges interest and penalty tax` `the days from the transfer until I pay` `the market rate` `default` `the Commissioner accepts it was not deliberate and I took reasonable care` (`my conduct, from my answers` `I told the Commissioner in writing before any audit` `I told the Commissioner in writing during an audit` `I obstructed an audit`)
    WHERE
        `default` MEANS
            IF `the failure was deliberate` THEN `a deliberate tax default` ELSE `a tax default that is not deliberate`

§§ `Foreign buyers -- refund of the surcharge (s 72(5))`

-- Situation: you paid the foreign ownership surcharge and have since become a citizen or permanent resident.

@export Must the Commissioner refund the foreign ownership surcharge to me if I apply (s 72(5))?
GIVEN `I paid the surcharge because I was a foreign person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid the foreign ownership surcharge because you were a foreign person when you acquired the interest
      `the date I acquired the interest`                    IS A DATE @desc The day you acquired the interest in the residential land (ISO 8601)
      `I have stopped being a foreign person`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since become an Australian citizen, a permanent visa holder or a New Zealand citizen with a special category visa
      `the date I stopped being a foreign person`           IS A DATE @desc The day you stopped being a foreign person (ISO 8601); otherwise any date
      `I still held the interest then`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you still held the interest in the land on the day you stopped being a foreign person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the surcharge be refunded to me` IS
    `the surcharge must be refunded on application (s 72(5))` `I paid the surcharge because I was a foreign person` `the date I acquired the interest` `I have stopped being a foreign person` `the date I stopped being a foreign person` `I still held the interest then`

§§ `The first home owner grant`

-- Situation: buying or building your first home in South Australia.

@export Is a first home owner grant payable to me, and how much is it (First Home and Housing Construction Grants Act 2000, ss 7, 18)? 0 if none is payable.
GIVEN `I am buying the home under a contract of sale`                                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying the home (with its land) under a contract of sale; answer no if you are having it built or building it yourself
      `I am building the home myself as an owner builder`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are building the home (or having it built) on your land without a comprehensive home building contract (an owner builder)
      `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has previously been occupied or sold as a place of residence (answer no for a brand-new home)
      `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home was substantially renovated and its sale to you is a taxable supply of new residential premises under the GST Act s 40-75(1)(b)
      `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home, as renovated, has been occupied or sold as a place of residence before your purchase
      `the commencement date`                                                          IS A DATE @desc The day the contract was made, or for an owner builder the day laying the foundations began (ISO 8601)
      `the transaction is complete`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transaction is complete: for a purchase, you are entitled to possession and the steps to register your title have been taken; for a building, it is ready to live in
      `the date of completion`                                                         IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction was (or will be) completed (ISO 8601)
      `the consideration`                                                              IS A NUMBER @desc The price of the home (for a purchase), the total price of the building work (for a building contract), or your actual costs excluding your own labour (for an owner builder), in Australian dollars
      `the Commissioner thinks the price may be below market value`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a purchase: whether the Commissioner considers the price may be less than the market value
      `the market value as the Commissioner determines it`                             IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of the home and land as the Commissioner determines it (used for a building contract, an owner builder, or a purchase the Commissioner thinks is under-priced), in Australian dollars; otherwise the price
      `the Commissioner thinks it is a scheme to get around the rules`                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is of the opinion the transaction forms part of a scheme to circumvent the grant's limits or requirements
      `every applicant is an individual`                                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-applicant is an individual (a natural person)
      `every applicant is 18 or older`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-applicant is at least 18 (or the Commissioner has exempted you)
      `at least one applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or at least one co-applicant is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident
      `an applicant or partner has had a grant before`                                 IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-applicant or a spouse or domestic partner of any of you was a party to an earlier first home owner grant application, in any State, on which a grant was paid (a separated spouse does not count)
      `that grant was repaid for not living in the home, with any penalty paid`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that earlier grant was paid back because the residence requirement or a condition was not met, and any s 39(3) penalty was paid
      `an applicant or partner could have had a grant on an earlier purchase`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-applicant or a partner could have successfully applied for a first home owner grant on an earlier transaction (or could have, had you then been a citizen or permanent resident)
      `an applicant or partner owned residential property before 1 July 2000`          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-applicant or a partner held a relevant interest (usually ownership) in residential property in Australia before 1 July 2000
      `an applicant or partner has owned residential property`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-applicant or a partner held a relevant interest (usually ownership) in residential property in Australia before the commencement date
      `whoever owned it lived in it for 6 months in a row`                             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether whoever owned that property lived in it as a place of residence for at least 6 months in a row (it matters only before the relevant day)
      `the relevant day for the grant`                                                 IS A DATE @desc The day section 4 of the Statutes Amendment (Budget Measures) Act 2025 came into operation (the deposited legislative history records 13 February 2025), as a date (ISO 8601)
      `every owner is applying`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether everyone who is, or on completion will be, an owner of the home is an applicant
      `the date I apply`                                                               IS A DATE @desc The day you apply (or applied) for the grant (ISO 8601)
      `the Commissioner allows my application outside the period`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has allowed your application before or after the application period
      `I have met the residence requirement, or the Commissioner pays in anticipation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have lived in the home for 6 months in a row as required, or the Commissioner is paying the grant before that, satisfied that you intend to
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `How much first home owner grant do I get` IS
    IF `the first home owner grant is payable (s 7)` `application` `I have met the residence requirement, or the Commissioner pays in anticipation`
    THEN `the amount of the first home owner grant (s 18)` `application`
    ELSE `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
    WHERE
        `application` MEANS `my grant application, from my answers` `I am buying the home under a contract of sale` `I am building the home myself as an owner builder` `the home has been lived in or sold as a home before` `it was substantially renovated and sold to me as new residential premises` `it has been lived in or sold since the renovation` `the commencement date` `the transaction is complete` `the date of completion` `the consideration` `the Commissioner thinks the price may be below market value` `the market value as the Commissioner determines it` `the Commissioner thinks it is a scheme to get around the rules` `every applicant is an individual` `every applicant is 18 or older` `at least one applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `an applicant or partner has had a grant before` `that grant was repaid for not living in the home, with any penalty paid` `an applicant or partner could have had a grant on an earlier purchase` `an applicant or partner owned residential property before 1 July 2000` `an applicant or partner has owned residential property` `whoever owned it lived in it for 6 months in a row` `the relevant day for the grant` `every owner is applying` `the date I apply` `the Commissioner allows my application outside the period`

-- The period opens on the commencement date (s 14(5)(a)); the Commissioner may allow an application outside it (s 14(6)).
@export By what date must I apply for the first home owner grant (s 14(5): 12 months after completion)?
GIVEN `the date of completion` IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction was (or will be) completed (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply for the grant` IS
    `the last day to apply (s 14(5)(b))` `the date of completion`

@export By what date must I begin living in the home as my principal place of residence for the first home owner grant (s 12)?
GIVEN `the date of completion`                                                           IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction was (or will be) completed (ISO 8601)
      `a longer completion period approved by the Commissioner for the grant, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If the Commissioner has approved a longer time to move in, its length in months from completion; otherwise 0
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I move in for the grant` IS
    `the last day to begin living in the home (s 12)` `the date of completion` `a longer completion period approved by the Commissioner for the grant, in months`

@export Until what date must I keep living in the home, without a break, for the first home owner grant (s 12)?
GIVEN `the date I moved in`                                                              IS A DATE @desc The day you began to live in the home as your principal place of residence (ISO 8601)
      `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner for the grant, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If the Commissioner has approved a residence period shorter than 6 months, its length in months; otherwise 0
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until when must I live in the home for the grant` IS
    `the day the residence period ends (s 12)` `the date I moved in` `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner for the grant, in months`

-- Situation: the grant was paid in anticipation and you will not live in the home as required. Not doing so is an
-- offence (maximum $5 000, s 20(4)) and the Commissioner may add a penalty up to the grant (s 39(3)).
@export If my first home owner grant was paid before I met the residence requirement and I will not meet it, by what date must I tell the Commissioner in writing and repay the grant (s 20(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the date of completion`                                                           IS A DATE @desc The day the transaction was (or will be) completed (ISO 8601)
      `a longer completion period approved by the Commissioner for the grant, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If the Commissioner has approved a longer time to move in, its length in months from completion; otherwise 0
      `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner for the grant, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc If the Commissioner has approved a residence period shorter than 6 months, its length in months; otherwise 0
      `the date it became clear I would not meet the requirement`                        IS A DATE @desc The day it first became apparent that you would not live in the home as required (ISO 8601); if it has not, a date after the time allowed
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I notify the Commissioner and repay the grant` IS
    `the last day to notify and repay (s 20(2), (3))` (`the end of the period allowed for compliance (s 20(3)(a))` `the date of completion` `a longer completion period approved by the Commissioner for the grant, in months` `a shorter residence period approved by the Commissioner for the grant, in months`) `the date it became clear I would not meet the requirement`

-- Situation: the Commissioner requires you to repay the grant.
@export What is the most penalty the Commissioner can impose, in dollars, if I must repay the first home owner grant (s 39(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the amount I must repay`                                IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the Commissioner requires you to repay, in Australian dollars
      `it was paid because of a false or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid because an applicant made a false or misleading statement
      `I did not make the repayment required`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have failed to make a repayment the Commissioner (or the grant's conditions) required
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most penalty if I must repay the grant` IS
    `the most penalty under s 39(2) and (3)` `the amount I must repay` `it was paid because of a false or misleading statement` `I did not make the repayment required`

@export What interest rate, per cent a year, applies if I repay the first home owner grant by instalments (Regulations 2015 reg 6)?
GIVEN `the market rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The market rate for the financial year, per cent a year (the May average of the 90-day Bank Accepted Bill Rate, or a rate the Minister gazettes), e.g. 4.35
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What interest rate applies to repaying the grant by instalments` IS
    `the interest rate on repayment by instalments, per cent a year (reg 6)` `the market rate`

-- Situation: you disagree with the decision on your grant application, or with a penalty under s 39.
@export By what date must I lodge an objection with the Treasurer against the Commissioner's decision on my grant application (s 25(3))?
GIVEN `the date of the notice of the decision`      IS A DATE @desc The date of the notice of the Commissioner's decision on your grant application (ISO 8601)
      `the date of a later retrospective provision` IS A DATE @desc If the decision was made in anticipation of a retrospective provision, the day it was enacted or made (ISO 8601); otherwise the same date as the notice
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I object to a grant decision` IS
    `the last day to object to a grant decision (s 25(3))` `the date of the notice of the decision` `the date of a later retrospective provision`

§§ `Challenging a stamp duty assessment (Taxation Administration Act 1996)`

-- Situation: you disagree with an assessment of stamp duty.

@export By what date must I lodge an objection with the Minister against a stamp duty assessment (Taxation Administration Act s 86)?
GIVEN `the date the assessment was served on me` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice of assessment was served on you (or you were notified of the decision), as a date (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I object to a duty assessment` IS
    `the last day to object (s 86)` `the date the assessment was served on me`

@export By what date must I appeal to the Supreme Court after the Minister determines my objection (Taxation Administration Act s 94(1))?
GIVEN `the date the determination was served on me` IS A DATE @desc The day notice of the Minister's determination of your objection was served on you (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I appeal to the Supreme Court` IS
    `the last day to appeal (s 94)` `the date the determination was served on me`

@export How much of the assessed duty must I pay before I can appeal, in dollars (Taxation Administration Act s 93)?
GIVEN `the duty assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc The duty assessed, not counting interest and penalty tax, in Australian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I pay before I can appeal` IS
    `the tax to be paid before appealing (s 93)` `the duty assessed`

§§ `Registering a car`

-- Situation: registering a vehicle, or transferring its registration into your name.

-- The s 71CB question's @desc covers a former partner after a breakdown the Commissioner accepts, so a yes is read as
-- qualifying (passed as current partners).
@export What stamp duty is payable when I apply to register a vehicle, or to transfer its registration into my name, in South Australia (s 42B, Schedule 2 clause 2)?
GIVEN `I am registering the vehicle`                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying to register (or renew the registration of) the vehicle; answer no if you are applying to transfer its registration into your name
      `it is a new vehicle with a list price`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle has never been registered anywhere and has a manufacturer's or distributor's list price in South Australia
      `the list price`                                         IS A NUMBER @desc The list price of the vehicle including GST, in Australian dollars (new vehicles only; otherwise 0)
      `the price of the optional equipment`                    IS A NUMBER @desc The list price (or, without one, the actual price including GST) of optional equipment such as a particular transmission or power steering, in Australian dollars; otherwise 0
      `I bought it second-hand`                                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are transferring the registration of a previously registered vehicle that you bought
      `the price I paid`                                       IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid for the vehicle, in Australian dollars (0 if it was not bought)
      `the market value of the vehicle`                        IS A NUMBER @desc What the vehicle might reasonably sell for in the open market, free of encumbrances, including GST, in Australian dollars
      `it is a commercial vehicle or a trailer`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a commercial motor vehicle or a trailer, as the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 defines them
      `it is a trailer that is not a heavy vehicle`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a trailer that is not a heavy vehicle
      `the registration period, in months`                     IS A NUMBER @desc The period of registration you are applying for, in months, counting part of a month as a month (12 for a year)
      `the registration period is 31 days or less`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the period of registration is 31 days or less
      `ad valorem duty already paid on buying it`              IS A NUMBER @desc Ad valorem stamp duty already paid or payable on another document by which the vehicle was transferred to you, in Australian dollars; otherwise 0
      `I am entitled to the s 38 reduced registration fee`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled under section 38 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 to register the vehicle at a reduced fee
      `I already have this exemption on another vehicle I own` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you already enjoy the s 38 duty exemption on another vehicle you currently own
      `I own the vehicle`                                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the owner of the vehicle
      `I hold a South Australian concession card`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a State concession card issued by the department responsible for the Family and Community Services Act 1972 (the class prescribed by Stamp Duties Regulations 2013 reg 14)
      `I hold a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a pensioner entitlement card issued under a Commonwealth law (for example a Pensioner Concession Card)
      `my card gives me reduced public transport fares`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that card entitles you to travel on public transport in South Australia at reduced fares
      `it comes to me from my spouse or domestic partner`      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the sole effect of the application is to transfer the registration between you and your spouse or domestic partner (current, or former after a breakdown the Commissioner accepts), or to register it in your name when your partner was its last registered owner
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `What duty is payable on registering my vehicle` IS
    IF `the vehicle application is exempt (s 71CB(2)(a)(ii), (b))` `it comes to me from my spouse or domestic partner` `spouses or domestic partners` FALSE
    THEN `the amount, in dollars, is` 0
    ELSE `the duty on the vehicle application (s 42B(1d))` `I am registering the vehicle` `value` `it is a commercial vehicle or a trailer` (`my registration period, from my answers` `the registration period, in months` `the registration period is 31 days or less`) (`my vehicle exemption facts, from my answers` `it is a trailer that is not a heavy vehicle` `ad valorem duty already paid on buying it` `I am entitled to the s 38 reduced registration fee` `I already have this exemption on another vehicle I own` `I own the vehicle` `I hold a South Australian concession card` `I hold a Commonwealth pensioner entitlement card` `my card gives me reduced public transport fares`)
    WHERE
        `value` MEANS `the value of the motor vehicle (s 42B(1))` (`the kind of my vehicle application, from my answers` `I am registering the vehicle` `it is a new vehicle with a list price` `I bought it second-hand`) `the list price` `the price of the optional equipment` `the price I paid` `the market value of the vehicle`
